ALBUKHR Project Market Technical Contract Alignment Audit
Version 1.0
Document ID: ALB-PMF-TCA-001
Version: 1.0
Status: Controlled Technical Audit Draft
Scope: Mainnet project/staking contract alignment
Date: 2026-10-02
1. Audit Objective
This audit checks whether the current Mainnet database, API and frontend staking/withdrawal contracts are aligned with the ALBUKHR Project Market Framework v1.
The audit is read-only. No project status, staking term, treasury row, stake row, or withdrawal record was modified by this audit.
2. Executive Result
The current system is not yet contract-aligned with the new Project Market Framework.
The most important findings are:
projects.project_code is the authoritative full project code in the current project registry, for example AZMAN-4080.
project_staking_terms.project_code currently uses base codes for six Core projects (AZMAN, LABBAIKA, BARSH, URBAN, KHAIRAT, HAUWAL) while RAHEEM-25 is already an exact match.
The current staking database contract requires an exact project-code match, so six current Core projects cannot satisfy the staking-term lookup after activation.
The current frontend still contains legacy base-code configuration and hard-coded duration logic.
The current database has zero stake rows, so there are currently no recorded Mainnet/Testnet stake positions that need term-preserving migration.
The current withdrawal request contract is a legacy/simple contract: it uses a fixed 1% fee, requires maturity, and checks the stored stakes.reward_amount / stakes.amount directly. It does not yet implement the full new project-specific withdrawal policy model.
Core liquidity settlement can auto-promote APPROVED -> ACTIVE when required liquidity is met and an exact staking term exists. This is compatible with the Core activation gate already hardened, but the broader Market Framework requires capability-specific readiness and should not remain dependent on legacy term structure.
No Mainnet project_treasury rows currently exist for the listed projects, so Core projects are not presently treasury-ready.
Conclusion: Do not migrate the current reward/term rows yet. First establish the canonical project/term contract and introduce the new versioned term model without breaking existing records.
