5. Critical Staking Lookup Finding
Current Mainnet public.create_stake_from_completed_payment(...) performs:
project lookup by p_project_id
requires Mainnet + Core + Core Slot 1..7
requires projects.status = 'active'
staking term lookup by exact:
st.project_code = v_project.project_code
st.network = 'mainnet'
st.duration_days = p_duration_days
st.active = true
Therefore:
AZMAN-4080 does not match AZMAN.
LABBAIKA-3980 does not match LABBAIKA.
BARSH-1125 does not match BARSH.
URBAN-5180 does not match URBAN.
KHAIRAT-3132 does not match KHAIRAT.
HAUWAL-6552 does not match HAUWAL.
RAHEEM-25 is the only current project whose project code and term code are already aligned.
Activation consequence
The hardened Core activation function also requires at least one active term for the exact project code. Thus the current mismatch intentionally blocks six of the Core projects from activation until the contract is aligned.
This is the correct fail-closed behavior, but the underlying term identity still needs to be redesigned before new production terms are created.
