7. Current API Contract
src/financial-gateway.js currently enforces:
Payment approval
Pi bearer authentication
verified Pi identity
exact project code lookup
Mainnet network
Core project type
Core slot 1..7
project must already be ACTIVE
treasury exists and is active/locked
Pi payment metadata matches amount/network/project code/duration
recipient matches project treasury wallet
Payment completion
The same checks are performed before the authoritative create_stake_from_completed_payment RPC is invoked.
This is appropriately server-authoritative, but it currently assumes the legacy term model and Core-only investment route.
Important architectural implication
The new Project Market Framework will eventually support project-specific terms and distinct Core/Internal/External business engines. The current payment route is therefore a Core-only legacy financial contract, not yet the final universal Project Market contract.
It should not simply be generalized by removing the Core check.
